PTLib 2.12-beta10 (OPAL stack): construct the pid-file streams from a char *

libstdc++ resolves std::ifstream's constructor over const char *,
std::filesystem::path and std::string.  PString converts implicitly to all
three, so the call is ambiguous under C++17 and later - the default standard for
GCC 11 and newer - and the three affected statements fail to compile.

Naming the conversion is the minimal repair and preserves the behaviour exactly:
PString::operator const char *() returns the same buffer the pre-C++17 overload
resolution used.

Applies to: 10503462abe31a6c288a39f6f894a5ceb367abbc (branch v2_12)
Upstream:   https://git.code.sf.net/p/opalvoip/ptlib

